WEBVTT

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.610
Sandbag ni

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.610
On the sandbag,

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.250
Guess it's time to say goodbye to this old shed.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.370
Huh? Yeah...

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.720
I thought that maybe one world champion would come from this worn-down shed.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.520
Yeah...

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:44.440
Guess that was no more than a dream.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.020
Now that our mainstay, Joe, can't hit the temple anymore...

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.980
But Joe's trying really hard to get over that!

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.980
It can't be done.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.620
All right, old man. I've got some deliveries to run.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.420
It's still only June... Why is it so hot out?

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.140
Is anybody home? This is Hayashiya!

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.400
Thanks for your time.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.060
Here you go.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.520
Thank you kindly for your business!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.270
No, thank you!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.700
Now, where do we go next...

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.390
Yabuki-kun!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:33.730
You knocked mine off!

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.270
Dammit, I'm off my game today!

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.190
Shut up!

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.230
I'm already fed up with being alone,

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.400
so don't go screaming like that!

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.660
Now listen! This is the only way...

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:45.660
that we can clear our minds!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.240
What are you talking about? You're just wasting time!

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:52.710
Shut up, kids! I'm trying to focus here!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.790
Let's see now...

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.300
Why is it so hot out...

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.800
<i>Sachi, there's no use complaining.</i>

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:07.590
Hey, how long do you plan on thinking? Just make a damn move already!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.840
Shut the hell up and let me think!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.680
Hey, look!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.690
Joe!

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:23.950
He's doing roadwork!

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.650
Okay guys, clear a path!

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:26.490
You got it!

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.410
D-Did you see his face?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.870
Yeah...

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.620
He lost to the champion <i>and</i> the top ranked boxer.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.210
Pretty disappointing, if you ask me.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:25.210
He used to talk about crossing Namida Bridge the other way, back in the day.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:29.210
But I guess he never made it all the way across.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.720
I guess the star of skid row is just stardust in the pros.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.480
Now ain't that miserable.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.230
What do you mean, "shh"!?

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:46.360
You're not trying to get a baby to piss here!

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.690
So he lost twice! Don't make such a fuss about it!

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.910
Every fighter gets into a trump sometimes!

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.030
I think you mean "slump," Sachi.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.910
Oh, yeah. Slump.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.740
He's in a slump!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.550
Okay, that's enough! Let's go!

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.550
Yeah!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:22.330
Joe... The spot you're hitting with all your might

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.790
is just about the height of Rikiishi's temple.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.830
I can tell.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.960
But Joe...

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.840
You can hit it all you like, but it's still a sandbag.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.180
Not a living person.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.100
If you can't hit a living person's temple in the ring,

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.600
then you're beyond all hope.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:03.810
D-Damn you, Rikiishi...

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.610
Rikiishi...

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.610
Damn you...

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.250
R-Rikiishi...

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:51.890
Nishi.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.360
Oh, welcome back.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:15.000
Well, Joe was punching it like mad,
 right around where the temple would be,

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.630
and the sandbag just couldn't handle it.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:37.730
He'd be overcome with anxiety if he didn't work out.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.280
That's enough, Nishi. You can stop sewing.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.140
You're home, old man?

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:13.640
Y-Yeah.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:17.030
I guess I fell asleep.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.950
Damn, my shoulders are freezing.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.870
Well, I'm gonna go to bed for real now.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:32.410
Sure.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:42.130
Oh, old man, I'm going to the Boxing Association alone tomorrow.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:43.590
Huh?

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:47.260
If I asked your permission, you wouldn't let me.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:51.600
Joe, what business do you have at the association?

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.850
Requesting a match. What else?

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:56.860
What?

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.400
A match?

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.730
That's right.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.230
With who?

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:06.950
If I can't fight the champion, Ozaki, or the top-ranked Harajima,

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.740
then I'll settle for the No. 2, Nango.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.740
Well, old man?

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.920
This is gonna be my final challenge.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.340
Final challenge?

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:04.710
I never thought he'd be the one coming here!

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:09.510
I guess that's the end for Yabuki Joe, the poor bastard.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.680
He's not even in satisfactory condition!

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.940
Another match could be lethal!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.980
I'm sure Tange knows that as well.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.190
That's why he's not here today.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:23.650
Well, why not let Yabuki have his way one last time?

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:29.120
Now we can finally rid the Japanese Boxing Association of the Grim Reaper.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.540
Precisely!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.380
Next week?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.880
Yes. I heard Yabuki requested it from the Association directly.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.970
That's insane!

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:53.970
He can't fight after that loss, not without time to recover!

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.560
This represents a huge problem.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.890
For me and for him.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.630
Don't worry, Miss Yohko.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:40.770
The name's Harry Robert, and I bring in the dollars.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:43.060
I stake my life on management.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.150
I'll bring you a very good boxer very soon!

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.360
You're sure about that?

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.400
Oh, yes! Just, just, just a moment, okay?

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:21.890
Joe! You don't need to go so fast!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:36.490
He's training far too hard.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:45.540
Yabuki-kun, you're the man that killed Rikiishi-kun.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.130
But I'm not going to let you ruin yourself.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:48.250
I swear it!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:12.150
If he keeps up this pace, he'll kill himself!

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:23.990
Let him be.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:28.590
Joe wants to do this till the day he dies.

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.890
Yay!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.890
<i>All right!</i>

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.390
Well, there goes the last of the sand.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:38.740
You're sure he's on this flight, Robert?

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:43.040
Don't you worry! I gave him a ticket before I came to Japan!

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.130
Hey! Carlos!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.380
Oh, Robert!

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:05.850
That's him?

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.140
Oh, yes!

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.600
Hey! Shiraki Yohko-san!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:11.350
Hello!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.980
Robert, it's the press. You handle the rest.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:15.820
Okay.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:20.070
How rare to see you here!

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:21.030
Who was that?

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.820
No one. I was just watching the planes.

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:26.080
Oh, really? The chairwoman of a boxing club watching planes?

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:26.790
Is that so funny?

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.450
Oh, no, not at all...

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.460
Oh, I get it now!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.380
You don't have to play games with me, Chairwoman!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:38.510
What do you mean?

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:41.430
That foreigner you were with is the international promoter Robert.

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:43.930
And the man in the sombrero must be...

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.560
Well, fine then. I'll fill you in.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:47.640
Really?

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:50.520
The man in the sombrero was recruited by our gym.

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.310
Huh? From what country?

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:54.020
What's his name?

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.780
I don't mean to hide it from you,

00:20:56.780 --> 00:21:00.150
but I'd rather you wait until the Joe-Nango match in two days.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.820
Joe-Nango match?

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:06.040
Yes. Yabuki Joe's match with Nango from Pacific Gym.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.160
Shiraki-san!

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:10.580
So much for a headline...

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:35.180
Let me be frank. It's hard for me to second your upcoming match.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.690
He doesn't have to fight if he can't finish his opponent off, does he?

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:42.910
Joe called this his final challenge.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:44.690
He's risking it all on this painful match.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.870
It may be a shameful match, but there's nothing we can do about it.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.660
I'll just have to watch his final match.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:58.170
I...

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.960
don't think it's painful or shameful at all.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:14.310
I haven't been fighting Ozaki, the champion.

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.650
Not the first-place Harajima.

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:19.150
And not the second-place Nango.

00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:26.030
I've been fighting Rikiishi. Rikiishi Toru.

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:28.620
And I'm going to keep fighting his ghost

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:32.530
until he tells me, "You win, Joe."

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:45.750
If I can't do that,

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:47.630
that's it for Yabuki Joe.

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:51.140
That's the law between me and Rikiishi.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:53.140
<i>The law...</i>

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:55.140
<i>The law!</i>

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:57.140
<i>The law!</i>

00:22:57.900 --> 00:23:02.150
<i>The law!</i>

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:43.360
Yuke kouya wo

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:43.360
Go to the wilderness!

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:47.150
Oira boxer

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:47.150
I am a boxer.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:54.910
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:54.910
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:00.580
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:00.580
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:03.000
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:03.000
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:09.210
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:09.210
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:12.220
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:12.220
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:16.470
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:16.470
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:20.230
Oira boxer

00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:20.230
I am a boxer.

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:28.440
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:28.440
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!

00:24:34.870 --> 00:24:38.410
As Joe faces his greatest crisis, he issues his final challenge:

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:40.120
The Joe-Nango match!

00:24:40.830 --> 00:24:44.500
A strange atmosphere hangs in the full house of Korakuen Hall.

00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:50.800
And the fighter invited by Shiraki Gym makes an unexpected introduction.

00:24:51.260 --> 00:24:55.840
His name is Carlos Rivera, also known as the Uncrowned Emperor!

00:24:56.640 --> 00:24:59.560
Sparks fly as Joe's and Carlos' eyes meet.

00:25:00.390 --> 00:25:05.570
Now, as Joe stands in the ring while taking in Carlos' sharp stare,

00:25:05.570 --> 00:25:07.240
which way is tomorrow!?
